        [
          "python",
          "The Accuracy Trap in Anomaly Detection\n============================================================\nDataset: 10000 samples, 200 anomalies (2.0%)\n\nModel                Accuracy     Precision    Recall     F1      \n------------------------------------------------------------\nAlways Normal        0.9800       0.0000       0.0000     0.0000  \nRandom (2%)          0.9608       0.0200       0.0200     0.0200  \nGood Detector        0.9920       0.8000       0.8000     0.8000  \n\nKey insight: 'Always Normal' has 98.0% accuracy\nbut detects ZERO anomalies!"
        ]
